{"audit": {"coverageKind": "diagnoses", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2009_zamora_gozalo_liñán:0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/1:diagnosis", "kind": "diagnosis", "path": "0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/1", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2009_zamora_gozalo_liñán", "subject": "parsleyi_zamora_2009", "text": "Eocrinid with globular−shaped theca and large, slightly\nconvex thecal plates (slightly ornamented). Epispires are\nsimple and numerous, with a well developed raised rim\nsometimes covered by a stereomic dome or by small plates.\nThecal plates are arranged into six or seven subregular\ncirclets. At least seven long, narrow biserial and spiralled\nbrachioles. Almost no stalk, except for an expanded holdfast\ncomposed of tiny globular plates.\n", "tree": "taxonomy"}
